From 17c411e09d121f6217f17eed2cca3c9f0afef76e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:47:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(od-sevev): envelope flap as its own layer
 (sheet_modal_body + 3-frame sheet_modal_flap)

The Animator's wave-B ask: the blue envelope's flap, baked into sheet_modal's
9-slice title band, now exists as a 3-frame strip (sealed V, lifting, open =
the band) over a flap-less sheet_modal_body. Body + flap f2 = sheet_modal,
pixel for pixel (asserted in wave9.py); sheet_modal is unchanged. The strip is
24 rows so the point's shadow stays one art row instead of stretching into a
slab in the 9-slice's centre. Pipeline re-import: 0 drift, 261 kit pieces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JZ6f2h5tcXVKGAwuAga5z8
