From e862992c628b2afd804a78b5ecc357e2cfe924ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:00:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(od-sevev): slipStamp cue for the ballot-slip stamp
 (audio v1.4)

A rubber-stamp thunk on the spin tag's slam f0 (the Animator's wave B): UI
bus, 89 ms, one unpitched file, burst -20.5 LUFS (2 dB under the stamp's
heard -18.5, 4.5 under the buy it lands with, centroid 0.69 kHz). Not
Herzog's stamp: no 2.5 kHz thump, ink glide or bell. One-line hook in
shop.gd where tagSlam starts (a no-op without the host or the cue), the
coverage scan entry, a cue test and a host-path test. Cue-spec v1.4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JZ6f2h5tcXVKGAwuAga5z8
---
